23:07.740 --> 23:11.620
So the fluid naturally wants to be completely still and totally uniform,

23:11.620 --> 23:14.940
but clearly, looking around the universe, it isn't still.

23:15.120 --> 23:16.660
We have galaxies, we have thoughts.

23:16.720 --> 23:17.660
Right, it's very active.

23:17.660 --> 23:22.660
So to prevent the math from just instantly collapsing into this boring, flat equilibrium,

23:23.300 --> 23:26.320
the paper introduces a constraint called the stiff limit.

23:26.460 --> 23:27.340
The stiff limit, yes.

