The author provides a theorem proving that all these coarse graining projections preserve

28:42.640 --> 28:45.120
what is known as entropy monotonicity.

28:45.400 --> 28:46.720
Entropy monotonicity.

28:46.880 --> 28:51.400
Meaning the thermodynamic arrow of time doesn't break just because we zoomed out.

28:51.500 --> 28:51.960
Exactly.

28:52.120 --> 28:55.600
The universe doesn't suddenly start running backward just because we blurred our vision.

28:55.600 --> 28:56.280
Right.

28:57.000 --> 29:02.360
The disorder still inevitably increases, bounded mathematically by the data processing inequality.

29:02.880 --> 29:07.160
The macroscopic system is still enslaved to the thermodynamic laws of the microscopic

29:07.160 --> 29:07.660
